# E7007 — 测试包辅助代码的运行时导入闭包
id: E7007
trigger_tool: conan|python
phase: testing|packaging
error_signature: "NameError: name .* is not defined|test_package.*build failed after package created"
severity: 1
category: conan-test-package-runtime
match_keywords: Conan test_package, helper import, NameError, package test build, runtime closure
title: Validate test_package helper imports on the executed path
root_cause: A test_package can pass recipe syntax and package creation while a helper function references a standard-library module that was never imported. The missing import appears only when the CI test-package path executes that helper, after the main package has already built.
affected_scope: Conan recipes whose test_package performs platform-specific compiler, linker, filesystem, or artifact discovery in Python helpers.
verification_cmd: Run the exact test_package build path used by CI and require the helper branch to execute; fail closed on NameError before claiming package validation.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: executed-helper-import-audit
rec_description: For every helper called by test_package build() or test(), inspect imports and run the branch under the same profile and environment as CI; do not treat conan create of the main package as sufficient.
rec_command: python -m py_compile test_package/conanfile.py && conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<windows-profile>
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: explicit-import-and-ci-path-execution
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: fail-closed-missing-import
fallback_description: If the helper path cannot be executed locally, preserve the unknown state and wait for platform evidence instead of declaring the test package passed.
fallback_command: python -m py_compile test_package/conanfile.py
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: diagnostic-only
forbid_1_pattern: claim.*test.*pass.*without.*test_package|catch.*NameError.*as.*skip|remove.*helper.*branch
forbid_1_reason: Main-package compilation does not exercise test_package helper code, and suppressing a NameError can leave consumer or target validation unexecuted.
forbid_1_consequence: CI may report a package artifact while the required consumer test never built or ran.
principles: R16,R29,R34
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
